# 20
#title Sign and notarize the macOS release build
#url https://github.com/MobileReality/lantern/pull/20
#branch feat/mac-sign-notarize
#base origin/main
#opened 2026-11-09
#head 018abd50509f7478ff6cb966aa9add98f977c1f3
#describe what The release workflow's macOS job signs the app with the Developer ID certificate, notarizes it, staples the ticket and checks it, in a protected release environment, only from a v* tag.
#describe what Signing and notarization are unrun: the first v* tag is the real test.
#describe before The macOS zip was ad hoc signed and not notarized, so Gatekeeper quarantined it.
#describe after The zip is built, signed inside out with hardened runtime, notarized, stapled, verified and then zipped under the same name.
#describe verified typecheck, lint and the full test suite pass; plutil and bash -n pass; sign ran ad hoc on a built app and notarize against a stub xcrun. No real signing or notarization ran.
+ build/entitlements.mac.inherit.plist
+ build/entitlements.mac.plist
+ scripts/mac-ci-keychain.sh
+ scripts/mac-sign-notarize.sh
+ test/release-workflow.test.ts
~ .github/workflows/release.yml
~ CONTRIBUTING.md
~ README.md
~ docs/installation.md
~ test/workflow-hygiene.test.ts
#order .github/workflows/release.yml
#order scripts/mac-sign-notarize.sh
#order scripts/mac-ci-keychain.sh
#order build/entitlements.mac.plist
#order build/entitlements.mac.inherit.plist
#order test/release-workflow.test.ts
#order test/workflow-hygiene.test.ts
#order CONTRIBUTING.md
#order docs/installation.md
#order README.md
#reason build/entitlements.mac.inherit.plist Helper apps and the bundled node only need JIT, so they get nothing else
#reason build/entitlements.mac.plist Hardened runtime blocks JIT, the microphone, the camera and Apple events unless the app asks for exactly those
#reason scripts/mac-ci-keychain.sh The runner has no keychain holding the certificate, so a throwaway one is built from the secret and always deleted
#reason scripts/mac-sign-notarize.sh Keeps the signing logic in one readable script that CI and the maintainer run the same way, instead of a long inline YAML
#reason test/release-workflow.test.ts A mistake in the signing job would leak a secret or ship an unsigned app, so its shape is pinned
#reason .github/workflows/release.yml Releases must ship an app Gatekeeper trusts, so signing and notarizing run in a protected environment, tag-only, with secrets scoped to single steps
#reason CONTRIBUTING.md The maintainer needs the environment, secrets, tag ruleset and local signing steps written down, without any real value
#reason README.md The download note still said the macOS app was ad hoc signed
#reason docs/installation.md Download and Releases told users the build was ad hoc; they now describe the signed build and how an older tag behaves
#reason test/workflow-hygiene.test.ts Secrets must never spread to other workflows or jobs, so every workflow is checked for them
#story A maintainer ships a signed macOS release
#step actor Maintainer
#file .github/workflows/release.yml
#step action pushes a v* tag and approves the release deployment
#file .github/workflows/release.yml
#file CONTRIBUTING.md
#step subject the macOS app in the release
#file scripts/mac-sign-notarize.sh
#file scripts/mac-ci-keychain.sh
#file build/entitlements.mac.plist
#below interaction People download Lantern-mac.zip and macOS asks only once to open it
#file docs/installation.md
#file README.md
#below consequence Ad hoc signed, quarantined by Gatekeeper => Developer ID signed, notarized and stapled
#story Nobody else can reach the signing secrets
#step actor Anyone starting the workflow
#file .github/workflows/release.yml
#step action runs it from a branch, a fork or a mismatched tag
#file test/release-workflow.test.ts
#step subject the signing job
#file test/workflow-hygiene.test.ts
#below interaction The job stops before any secret is delivered
#below consequence Release job had no guard on the ref => Only a v* tag in the release environment signs
